{
  "rules": [
    "Correct for severe upward bias: The model consistently overestimates prices by 15-30 EUR after the peak at 98.01, failing to anticipate the magnitude of the crash.",
    "Reduce forecast lag: The model exhibits a slow mean-reversion response, predicting a gradual decline while the true market drops sharply within 3-5 days.",
    "Adjust for volatility overshoot: The model assumes a smooth, monotonic path and fails to capture the high-frequency oscillations (volatility) present in the true outcome.",
    "Incorporate sentiment triggers: Despite zero sentiment scores, the model ignores the structural regime shift from bull to bear market; apply a negative sentiment multiplier immediately after a price peak >95 EUR.",
    "Shorten horizon sensitivity: Errors are most pronounced in the first 10 days of the forecast horizon; apply a steeper initial decay rate to the forecast curve."
  ]
}
